  "body": "Goal: Browse the built-in holder library in the tool library window, grouped by taper, with the tools that use each holder.\n\nParent: #3663. Plan: the implementation plan in the #3663 comment. This is PR U6 of 11.\n\nFiles:\n- Add `tool_library_dialog/holders.rs`. It lists `holder_library::library()` grouped by taper, with a used-by count. The taper of the mounted machine comes first. The holder view is read-only: the outline from `drawing.rs`, and \"tools that use this holder\".\n- Add `tool_body::tools_using_holder(world, entry) -> Vec<String>` in `crates/app/src/tool_body.rs`. It reads the world, so it belongs in app. The key is `HolderRef.entry`.\n\nTests (new): `layout_window_holders`. `tool_library_holders::the_used_by_count_counts_tools_by_entry` in `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders.rs`. `tool_library_holders_ui::a_holder_lists_the_tools_that_use_it`.\n\nDepends on: U1 (#3892) and U4 (#3895, for the link from a holder to its tools). U3 supplies the drawing.\n\nCommands: none. Read only. No MCP tool is owed: `get_job` already shows each tool's `holder.library`.\n\nExpected quick gate: 10 steps for the UI, plus `app/tool_body.rs` (not measured).\n\nDone means: the Holders list shows holders by taper with a correct used-by count. A holder view lists its tools and draws the outline.\n\nChangelog row: The tool library window lists the built-in holders by taper, with the tools that use each one.\n",
